course: dictionary
lesson: 14956
title: Changing your mind
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When someone says no for a long time and then says yes, we say they relented. «After weeks of asking, Dad finally relented and bought us a puppy.» Relent means to give in, or to become less strict.
explain: Relent can also be about weather or pain. «The wind relented, and the sea grew calm.» The wind did not stop completely: it just became less strong. Ask yourself: did something strong become gentler or weaker?
explain: Look at the clue words around relent. If the sentence says «refused to relent», the person kept saying no and did not change their mind. If it says «finally relented», the change came at last, after waiting.
fact: «Relent» is a verb: relent, relents, relented, relenting.
fact: «Relent» means to give in after first saying no, or to become less strict.
fact: «Relent» can also mean that rain, wind or pain becomes less strong.
fact: «Refused to relent» means someone kept saying no and did not change their mind.
fact: Check your meaning by swapping in «gave in» or «became less strong» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «After weeks of asking, Dad finally relented and bought us a puppy.» What does relented mean here? | Went out to play | *Gave in and agreed | Ate all the cake | Shouted loudly
exercise: «The wind relented, and the waves grew calm.» What happened to the wind? | It stopped the boats from sailing | *It became less strong | It turned into snow | It grew stronger and louder
exercise: Which phrase means the teacher kept saying no and did not change her mind? | the rain relented | finally relented | *refused to relent | let us go out
test: «The storm relented at last, and the boats could sail home.» What does relent mean in this sentence? | Got stronger | Turned into sand | Sang loudly | *Became less strong
test: «Grandma would not relent, so we had to tidy our rooms first.» What does «would not relent» tell you about Grandma? | She lost her glasses | She went to sleep | She agreed at once | *She kept her answer firm
exam: «After a long wait, the king relented and let the villagers keep their fields.» What does relented mean? | Stayed the same | Left the village | *Gave in and changed his mind | Became angry
